{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"bfb0c87a087f143d5d4fb3c3b303347e581f98d0"},"timestamp":1519661247,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMDAyOTcwOTU=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2230","origin":"github"},"title":"create-sibling --existing=reconfigure  should git-annex init remote if local has git-annex and remote doesn't","message":"#### What is the problem?\nIn preparation to 0.10 release, I would need to migrate some datasets from pure git into annex.  Logical way to propagate those changes would be to `create-sibling --existing=reconfigure ` or alike to remote end also becomes git-annex repos.  But apparently even in reconfigure mode we just complain that it is not annex and do not initialize it: e.g. how it looks in master (in 0.9.x a bit different but to the same extent)\n\n```shell\n$\u003e datalad --dbg create-sibling --inherit -s datalad-public --existing=reconfigure\n[INFO   ] Connecting ...                                               \n[INFO   ] Considering to create a target dataset /mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms at /srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms of datasets.datalad.org \n[INFO   ] Target path /srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms already exists. And it fails to rmdir (rmdir: failed to remove ���/srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms���: Directory not empty). Will only reconfigure \n[INFO   ] Updating dataset '/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms' ... \n[INFO   ] Inherited publish_depends from \u003cDataset path=/mnt/btrfs/datasets/datalad/crawl/dicoms\u003e: ('refs/heads/*', 'refs/tags/*', 'refs/heads/*') \n[INFO   ] Configure additional default publication refspec \"refs/heads/*\" \n[INFO   ] Configure additional default publication refspec \"refs/tags/*\" \n[INFO   ] Configure additional default publication refspec \"refs/heads/*\" \n[INFO   ] Failed to enable annex remote datalad-public, could be a pure git \n[WARNING] Failed to determine if datalad-public carries annex. \n.: datalad-public(-) [ssh://datasets.datalad.org/srv/datasets.datalad.org/www/dicoms/dartmouth-phantoms (git)]\n[INFO   ] Adjusting remote git configuration \n[INFO   ] Enabling git post-update hook ... \n[INFO   ] Running post-update hooks in all created siblings \ncreate_sibling(ok): . (dataset)\n\n```\nso it seems I would need to `git annex init ` on remote manually for now","files":null}]}